course: dictionary
lesson: 4254
title: Grasslands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Grassland is a large area of land covered mostly with grass and few trees. Grasslands are a type of habitat, also called a biome, and they are found on many continents. Prairies, savannas and steppes are all kinds of grassland.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Lions rest for up to about 20 hours a day, hunt mostly from dusk to dawn and live mainly on African grassland and savanna, not in jungles.» The words «not in jungles» tell you grassland is a different place from a jungle, with far fewer trees.
explain: Rainfall is another clue. «Grasslands get too little rain for forests but too much for deserts.» So grasslands sit between two other homes. Compare them with forests, deserts and wetlands, and ask what each one is like.
fact: Grassland means a large area of land covered mostly with grass and few trees.
fact: Grasslands are habitats, also called biomes, and they are found on many continents.
fact: Prairies, savannas and steppes are all types of grassland.
fact: Animals such as bison, zebras and lions live on grasslands.
fact: Much farmland was once grassland.
exercise: «Lions live mainly on African grassland and savanna, not in jungles.» Where do lions mainly live? | *On African grassland and savanna | In jungles | In deep ocean caves | In the Arctic tundra
exercise: «Grasslands get too little rain for forests but too much for deserts.» What does this tell you about the rain on grasslands? | They are always flooded | They get more rain than forests | *They get a middle amount of rain | They get no rain at all
exercise: «Old Man Kangaroo is chased from the middle of Australia, mostly hot desert and dry grassland.» Which two habitats does this sentence name? | Rainforest and coast | Forest and river | Snowy tundra and ocean | *Hot desert and dry grassland
test: What is a grassland? | A thick forest of tall trees | A place covered in snow all year | A dry lake bed | *A large area of land covered mostly with grass and few trees
test: Which home fits the burrowing owl, according to the owl sentence? | Old forests along rivers | *Open grassland | Deep sea | Arctic tundra
exam: Which statement is true? | Grasslands have more trees than forests | *Lions live mainly on African grassland and savanna | Grasslands are wet all year round | Lions live mainly in jungles
